import Submission.Work.DSM4p.Lvl
import Submission.Work.DSM4p.Basic

/-!
# DSM4p — Route U: the plan for the transfer to the untilted levels

This module contains **no declarations**: it is the written plan that every lemma of the Route U
transfer (`Submission/Work/DSM4p/Lvl.lean` and its siblings) should be proved against.  It is in
the `depends_on` of every requested lemma of this subproject, so that the prover sees it.

## The setting

`B : Type a` is a commutative ring, `p` prime, `[Fact ¬IsUnit (p : B)]`,
`[IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {(p : B)}) B]`, `Q : DSMap.PerfectoidData p B` and
`hgr : IsRootSystem p gr` (i.e. `gr (k+1)^p = gr k`).  Write

* `B♭ := PreTilt B p = Perfection (B ⧸ (p)) p` (a perfect ring of characteristic `p`);
* `g♭ := tiltTower gr hgr`, `ϖ♭ := tiltTower Q.ϖ Q.root` (`Work.DSM4p.tiltTower`) — these are
  compatible systems of `p`-power roots in `B♭` (`tiltTower_isRootSystem`);
* `lvlP N := chartRing (tiltTower_isRootSystem gr hgr) (tiltTower Q.ϖ Q.root) N` — the
  characteristic-`p` chart level, a `B♭`-subalgebra of `B♭[1/g♭ 0]`, generated by
  `x♭_j(N) = ϖ♭_j^N / g♭_j`;
* `lvl N := untiltOf (lvlP N) (algebraMap B♭ (lvlP N)) = 𝕎(lvlP N) ⧸ I_N` where
  `I_N := 𝕎(lvlP N)·𝕎(algebraMap B♭ (lvlP N))(ker θ_B)` — the **untilted level**, a `B`-algebra
  via `lvlAlg Q hgr N` (an instance), with transition `lvlTr Q hgr N` (a ring hom) and
  `lvlTrAlg Q hgr N` (its `B`-linear version); `iterTr (lvlTrAlg Q hgr) n c` is the `c`-fold
  composite.

The final levels of the node are `D n := AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : lvl n)}) (lvl n)`, and
the assembly applies `Work.DSM4p.perfectoidData_adicCompletion` (the `PerfectoidData` structure,
with `QD.ϖ k = algebraMap B _ (Q.ϖ k)`) and `Work.DSM4p.isQRETp_adicCompletion` (the `IsQRETp`
transfer) to the tower of `lvl`s.

## The two estimates we start from (both PROVED, `Submission/Work/DSM4p/kerP.lean`,
`cokerP.lean`)

Over a perfect characteristic-`p` ring `R` with root systems `G`, `T`:

* `Work.DSM4p.kerP (hG) (hT) (hT0 : IsSMulRegular R (T 0)) (k M N) (hN : M*p^(k+2) ≤ N) (x : R)
  (hx : algebraMap R (chartRing hG T N) x ∈ Ideal.span {(algebraMap R _ (T 0))^M}) :
  T (k+1) * G (k+1) * x ∈ Ideal.span {T 0 ^ M}` — the char-`p` kernel (Hartogs) estimate;
* `Work.DSM4p.cokerP (hG) (hT) (k N) (r : chartRing hG T (N + p^(k+1))) :
  ∃ b : R, ∃ s ∈ chartLevel hG T N, algebraMap (G k) * r = algebraMap b + algebraMap (T 0 ^ p) * s`
  — the char-`p` cokernel (monomial) estimate at `m = 1`;
* `Work.DSM4p.cokerP_pow` — the generalisation of `cokerP` to a modulus `(T 0)^(p*m)` and a level
  shift `c ≥ p^(k+1)*m` (proved by copying `cokerP`/`cokerP_mono` with `m` inserted).

## The transfer tools from DSM5c (all at `Type a`, under `Work.DSM5c.Eta.U` / `G2.U`)

* `DSM5c.G2.U.surjective_fontaineTheta_of_perfectoidData Q` — `θ_B` is onto (`Work.DSM4p.surjective_fontaineTheta`);
* `DSM5c.Eta.U.teich_algebraMap hθ φ y : untiltOf.mk φ (teichmuller p (φ y)) = untiltOf.algebraMap hθ φ (♯y)`;
* `DSM5c.Eta.U.untilt_tiltOf` / `untilt_tiltTower` — `♯(tiltTower r hr k) = r k`, in particular
  `♯(g♭ k) = gr k`, `♯(ϖ♭ k) = Q.ϖ k`;
* `DSM5c.mem_span_p_sup_map_ker_fontaineTheta Q hθ φ` — for `R = lvlP N` perfect of char `p`
  (needs the instance `CharP (lvlP N) p`, see `Work.DSM4p.lvlP_charP`),
  `x ∈ (p : 𝕎R) ⊔ span(𝕎φ '' ker θ_B) ↔ constantCoeff x ∈ (φ (tiltVarpi Q))^p`;
  note `ϖ♭ 0 = tiltVarpi Q` (`tiltTower_zero` + the definition of `DSM5c.tiltVarpi`);
* `WittVector.ker_constantCoeff` (`𝕎R` for `R` perfect of char `p`: `ker constantCoeff = (p)`),
  `WittVector.map_teichmuller`, `WittVector.teichmuller_coeff_zero`, `WittVector.mem_span_p_pow_iff_le_coeff_eq_zero`;
* `DSM5c.Regularity.tiltVarpi_isSMulRegular Q` — `ϖ♭ 0` is a nonzerodivisor of `B♭`;
* `DSM5c.G2.U.isSMulRegular_untiltOf_of_regular Q hθ φ hp0 hc` — the untilt of a perfect char-`p`
  `B♭`-algebra with `(p : R) = 0` and `φ (tiltVarpi Q)^p` a nonzerodivisor is `p`-torsion-free.

## The mathematical steps

**(0) `p` vanishes in every level.** `(p : lvlP Q hgr N) = 0` is `map_natCast` + `CharP.cast_eq_zero`
of `B♭`.  If additionally `gr 0 ≠ 0`, then `g♭ 0 ≠ 0` (apply `♯` and use `PreTilt.untilt 0 = 0`,
`untilt_tiltTower`), and since `B♭` is reduced, `B♭[1/g♭ 0]` and all its subalgebras `lvlP N` are
nontrivial; then `CharP (lvlP N) p` is `CharP.charP_iff_prime_eq_zero hp` (`Work.DSM4p.lvlP_charP`).

**(1) `lvl_torsionFree`.** `isSMulRegular_untiltOf_of_regular Q hθ φ hp0 hc` with `R := lvlP N`,
`φ := algebraMap B♭ (lvlP N)`, `hp0` as in (0), and `hc : IsSMulRegular (lvlP N) (φ (tiltVarpi Q)^p)`
obtained from `tiltVarpi_isSMulRegular Q` (localisation of a nonzerodivisor, restriction to the
subalgebra).  **No hypothesis on `gr 0` is needed.**

**(2) Teichmüller representatives.** `lvl N = 𝕎R ⧸ I`, `I = ker (untiltOf.mk φ)`.
For `r : R`, `WittVector.ker_constantCoeff` gives `x - teichmuller p (constantCoeff x) ∈ (p)`, so
every class is congruent to `mk (teichmuller p r)` modulo `p` (`lvl_exists_teich`); and
`mk (teichmuller p r) ∈ (p : lvl N) ↔ r ∈ (φ (tiltVarpi Q))^p` (`lvl_teich_mem_span_p`), by
combining `Ideal.Quotient`-membership with `mem_span_p_sup_map_ker_fontaineTheta`
(`mk⁻¹ ((p : lvl)) = (p : 𝕎R) ⊔ I`).

**(3) `lvl_kernel`.** `x ∈ B` with `algebraMap B (lvl N) x ∈ (p^m : lvl N)`, `m*p^(k+m+3) ≤ N`
imply `Q.ϖ k * gr k * x ∈ (p^m : B)`.  **Proof (the dévissage that makes `p^m` work):**
let `S(1,L)` be the statement "`b ∈ B`, `algebraMap b ∈ (p : lvl N)` ⟹ `∃ c ∈ B, ϖ_{L+1} g_{L+1} b = p c`".
*Proof of `S(1,L)` (m = 1):* take `x♭ : B♭` with `♯x♭ ≡ x mod p` (PB2 dictionary, `DSM5c`/`DSPB2`:
`B ⧸ p ≅ B♭ ⧸ (ϖ♭ 0)^p`); `teich_algebraMap` gives
`mk (teichmuller (φ x♭)) = algebraMap (♯ x♭) ≡ algebraMap x mod p`, so
`mk (teichmuller (φ x♭)) ∈ (p : lvl N)`; by (2),
`φ x♭ ∈ (φ (tiltVarpi Q))^p = (φ (ϖ♭0))^p` in `lvlP N`; `kerP` with `G := g♭`, `T := ϖ♭`,
`M := p`, index `L` (bound `p·p^(L+2) ≤ N`) then gives `ϖ♭(L+1)·g♭(L+1)·x♭ ∈ (ϖ♭0 ^ p)` in `B♭`;
applying the ring hom `♯` and multiplying by the unit `v` (`Q.unit`: `Q.ϖ 0^p = p·v`) gives
`Q.ϖ (L+1)·gr (L+1)·♯x♭ ∈ (p : B)`; and `x ≡ ♯x♭ mod p` upgrades this to `x`.
*Dévissage:* given `algebraMap x ∈ (p^m : lvl N)`, apply `S(1, L)` with `L := k+m-1` to `x`, giving
`a x = p b₁` with `a := ϖ_{k+m} g_{k+m}` and `b₁ ∈ B`; torsion-freeness of `lvl N`
(`lvl_torsionFree`) and `algebraMap x ∈ p^m` give `algebraMap b₁ ∈ p^(m-1) lvl N`; iterate `m`
times (the `j`-th step uses `S(1,L)` again, the element `b_j ∈ B` and `algebraMap b_j ∈ p^(m-j) lvl`).
Result: `a^m x = p^m b_m` with `b_m ∈ B`, i.e. `a^m x ∈ (p^m : B)`.  Finally
`ϖ_k g_k = (ϖ_{k+m} g_{k+m})^(p^m) = a^m · a^(p^m - m)` because `m ≤ p^m`, so
`ϖ_k g_k x = a^(p^m-m)·(a^m x) ∈ (p^m : B)`.

**(4) `lvl_cokernel` / `lvl_cokernel_one`.**  For `y : lvl (n+c)` one has
`algebraMap B (lvl n) (ϖ_k g_k) · iterTr (lvlTrAlg Q hgr) n c y - algebraMap B (lvl n) x ∈ (p^m : lvl n)`
for some `x : B`, with `c` depending only on `m, k`.  Route:
* `iterTr (lvlTr Q hgr) n c (mk (Y)) = mk (𝕎(iterTr (chartTr …) n c) Y)` — the functoriality of
  `untiltOf.map` under composition; in particular the transition **fixes Teichmüller classes**:
  `iterTr (lvlTrAlg Q hgr) n c (mk (teichmuller p r)) = mk (teichmuller p r)` for `r ∈ lvlP (n+c)`
  (the chart transitions are the inclusions, `chartTr` is `Subalgebra.inclusion`, and
  `WittVector.map_teichmuller`).
* For a *monomial* `r = b₀ · x♭_J(N+c)^I ∈ lvlP (N+c)`, the char-`p` estimate `cokerP_pow` over
  `R := B♭`, `G := g♭`, `T := ϖ♭` gives
  `ϖ♭k·g♭k·r = b + (ϖ♭0)^(p·m)·s` with `b ∈ B♭`, `s ∈ lvlP N`; applying `teich`/`mk` and
  `teich_algebraMap`/`untilt_tiltTower` turns this into
  `algebraMap (ϖ_k g_k)·mk (teich r) = algebraMap (ϖ_k · ♯b) + algebraMap (p^m · …)·mk (teich s)`,
  hence `≡ algebraMap (ϖ_k ♯b) mod p^m`.  In Bhatt's second case (`b` is literally in `B♭`) the
  same computation gives an element of `B` (with the `(T 0)^(p·m)`-term zero).
* `lvlP (N+c)` is generated by `B♭` and the chart generators, so `chartLevel_mem_aeval_range` +
  the additivity of the decomposition assembles the monomial statements into
  `lvl_cokernel_one` (with `c = p^(k+1)`, `m = 1`) and, via `cokerP_pow`, into the general `m`.
* To pass from a Teichmüller class to an arbitrary `y : lvl (n+c)`: either use the Teichmüller
  representatives of (2) (which only give a mod-`p` statement, so the `m > 1` case must go through
  the *generalised* `cokerP_pow` as above), or use that
  `Ideal.span ({(p : 𝕎R)} ∪ Set.range (WittVector.teichmuller p)) = ⊤`
  (`Work.DSM4p.witt_span_p_teich`) together with the fact that the target
  `image(B) + p^m·lvl n` is an ideal of `lvl n`: this reduces the statement for `𝕎ψ(Y)`,
  `Y ∈ 𝕎(lvlP (n+c))`, to its generators `p` and `teich r`, `r ∈ lvlP (n+c)`.

**(4b) The `lvl_cokernel_step` route: reduce to the generators of `𝕎 R'`.**  Fix `n`, put
`c := p^(k+1)·m`, `a := teichmuller p (φ (ϖ♭k · g♭k)) ∈ 𝕎 (lvlP Q hgr n)` (so
`mk a = algebraMap B (lvl n) (Q.ϖ k * gr k)` by `teich_algebraMap` and `untilt_tiltTower`) and
`ψ := iterTr (chartTr g♭ ϖ♭) n c`.  Then the set

  `J := {Z : 𝕎 (lvlP Q hgr (n+c))  |  ∃ x : B, mk (a · 𝕎ψ Z) - algebraMap B (lvl n) x ∈ (p^m)}`

is an **ideal**:

* `mk (a·𝕎ψ(Z₁+Z₂)) = mk (a·𝕎ψZ₁) + mk (a·𝕎ψZ₂)` (additivity of the ring hom `mk ∘ (a·) ∘ 𝕎ψ`);
* `mk (a·𝕎ψ(Z₁Z₂)) = mk (a·𝕎ψZ₁) · mk (𝕎ψZ₂)`: with `mk (a·𝕎ψZ₁) = algebraMap x₁ + δ₁`, `δ₁ ∈ p^m`,
  the product is `algebraMap x₁ · mk (𝕎ψZ₂) + δ₁·mk (𝕎ψZ₂)`; the second term lies in `p^m`, and the
  first lies in the *ideal* `image(B) + p^m·lvl n` (it contains `image(B)`) — so it can be written
  as `algebraMap x' + δ'` with `δ' ∈ p^m`, which is exactly membership in `J`.

Moreover `1 ∈ J` (`mk a = algebraMap (ϖ_k g_k) ∈ image(B)`), and `J` contains `p` (since
`mk (a·p) = mk a · algebraMap (p) ∈ image(B)`) and `teich r` for every `r : lvlP Q hgr (n+c)`, so
`Ideal.span ({p} ∪ Set.range teich) ≤ J`; by `Work.DSM4p.witt_span_p_teich` that span is `⊤`
(trivially: `teich 1 = 1`), so `J = ⊤` and the statement holds for **every** `Z`, hence for every
`y : lvl Q hgr (n+c)`.

The only real input is `Z = teich r`: there `mk (a · teich r) = mk (teich (ϖ♭k·g♭k·r))`, and
`Work.DSM4p.cokerP_pow` writes `ϖ♭k·g♭k·r = b + (T 0)^(p·m)·s`, `b ∈ B♭`, `s ∈ lvlP Q hgr n`; then

  `teich (b + (T 0)^(p·m)·s) = teich b + teich ((T 0)^(p·m)·s) + ε`,  `ε ∈ (p : 𝕎 (lvlP Q hgr n))`

(the `constantCoeff` of `ε` is `(b + (T0)^{pm}s) - b - (T0)^{pm}s = 0`, so
`WittVector.ker_constantCoeff` applies), and
`mk (teich ((T 0)^(p·m)·s)) = algebraMap (Q.ϖ 0)^(p·m)·mk (teich s) = algebraMap (p^m·v^m)·mk (teich s)`
lies in `p^m·(lvl n)` by `Q.unit`.  Finally `mk ε ∈ (p : lvl n) ⊆ image(B) + p^m·(lvl n)`, because
`p = algebraMap B (lvl n) (Q.ϖ 0 ^ p · v) ∈ image(B)` and `image(B) + p^m·lvl n` is an *ideal* of
`lvl n`.  Hence `∃ x, mk (a·teich r) - algebraMap x ∈ (p^m)`, i.e. `teich r ∈ J`.

**(5) Merging the constants.** `Work.DSM4p.qretKernel_mono` / `qretCoker_mono` show that both
clauses of `IsQRETAt` are monotone in the pro constant `c`, so a single
`c := max (kernel constant) (cokernel constant)` gives `IsQRETp p B Q.ϖ gr (fun n => lvl Q hgr n) (lvlTrAlg Q hgr)`
(`lvl_isQRETp`).

**(6) Frobenius conditions on the levels.**
* `lvl_frobSurj` (`hs` of `perfectoidData_adicCompletion`): for `y : lvl N` take `r` with
  `y ≡ mk (teich r) mod p` (2), a `p`-th root `r'` of `r` (`PerfectRing (lvlP N) p`,
  `Work.DSM4p.chartLevel_perfect`), and `z := mk (teich r')`; then
  `z^p = mk (teich (r'^p)) = mk (teich r) ≡ y mod p`.
* `lvl_frobInj` (`hi`): for `y^p ∈ (p : lvl N)`, use (2) to write `y = mk (teich r) + p·w`; then
  `mk (teich (r^p)) ≡ y^p ≡ 0 mod p`, so `r^p ∈ (φ ϖ♭0)^p` by (2); perfectness of `lvlP N` gives
  `r ∈ (φ ϖ♭0)`, i.e. `r = φ(ϖ♭0)·r₁`, whence `mk (teich r) ∈ (mk (teich (φ ϖ♭ 0)))`; and
  `mk (teich (φ ϖ♭0)) = algebraMap (♯ ϖ♭0) = algebraMap (Q.ϖ 0)` by `teich_algebraMap` +
  `untilt_tiltVarpi`.  Finally `p ∈ (algebraMap (Q.ϖ 0))` because `p = Q.ϖ 0^p · v⁻¹` (`Q.unit`),
  so `y = mk (teich r) + p·w` lies in the ideal.

**(7) `lvl_dvd`.** `g♭0 · x♭_0(n) = ϖ♭0^n` in `lvlP n` (`chartGen_mul_gr` at the generator `k = 0`);
applying `teich` and `mk`, and `teich_algebraMap` (with `♯(g♭0) = gr 0`, `♯(ϖ♭0^n) = Q.ϖ 0^n`),
gives `algebraMap (gr 0) · mk (teich (x♭_0 n)) = algebraMap (Q.ϖ 0)^n`; since `Q.unit` gives
`Q.ϖ 0 ^ p = p·v` with `v : Bˣ`, we have `algebraMap (Q.ϖ 0)^n = (p : lvl n)^n · algebraMap (v)^n`
(`ϖ_0^n = ϖ_0^{pn}·(ϖ_0^{n(p-1)})`), so
`y := mk (teich (x♭_0 n)) · algebraMap (ϖ_0)^{n(p-1)} · (algebraMap v)^(-n)` works.

**Note on the hypotheses of `lvl_kernel`, `lvl_exists_teich`, `lvl_teich_mem_span_p`,
`lvl_frobSurj`, `lvl_frobInj`, `lvl_cokernel`:** each carries `hgr0 : gr 0 ≠ 0`.  This is not
decoration: `CharP (lvlP Q hgr N) p` requires `Nontrivial (lvlP Q hgr N)`
(`CharP.charP_iff_prime_eq_zero`), which is exactly what `gr 0 ≠ 0` provides
(`Work.DSM4p.lvlP_charP`); when `gr 0 = 0` the level is the zero ring and the characteristic-`p`
hypotheses are simply false there.  The case `gr 0 = 0` is handled separately in the assembly
(`Work.DSM4p.areaM4p_gr_zero`).

**(8) The assembly** (`Submission/Work/DSM4p/Main.lean`, written by the area owner): three cases.
* `IsUnit (p : B)`: `B` is a subsingleton (`IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {p}) B` with
  `Ideal.span {p} = ⊤`), so `D := fun _ => B`, `QD := fun _ => Q`, `tr := fun _ => AlgHom.id B B`,
  divisibility by `Subsingleton.elim`, and `IsQRETp` by `Work.DSM4p.isQRETp_self`.
* `gr 0 = 0`: then `gr k = 0` for all `k` (`Work.DSM2p.isReduced Q`), so the levels
  `lvl N` are subsingletons (or simply take the zero ring) and every clause is trivial.
* otherwise (`¬ IsUnit p`, `gr 0 ≠ 0`): the Route U tower
  `D n := AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : lvl n)}) (lvl n)`, with `PerfectoidData` from
  `perfectoidData_adicCompletion`, `IsQRETp` from `isQRETp_adicCompletion`, the divisibility
  pushed from `lvl_dvd` along `AdicCompletion.of`, and the `ϖ`-compatibility by construction.

-/
